{
  "$comment": [
    "Measured baselines, not targets. Every number here came from a run of",
    "tools/verify-size-budget.mjs against the PACKED tarballs of the Phase 9",
    "slice. docs/architecture/05-performance-budgets.md forbids inventing a",
    "budget before there is something to weigh, and Phase 9 is the first phase",
    "with components in it.",
    "",
    "  packed          the .tgz a consumer downloads (npm pack)",
    "  raw/gzip/brotli one entry point inside that tarball, gzip at level 9 and",
    "                  brotli at quality 11 — what a CDN would serve",
    "",
    "A package or entry point with no entry here FAILS the gate rather than",
    "escaping it: a budget file that covers only what somebody remembered to add",
    "reports coverage it does not have. Growth past tolerancePercent fails; a",
    "shrink passes and prints a reminder to lower the committed number.",
    "",
    "tolerancePercent absorbs the one part of this that is not bit-stable — tar",
    "headers carry file mtimes, so the packed figure can move by a byte or two on",
    "another machine. The axes measured out of the archive are deterministic.",
    "",
    "Re-baseline deliberately, in the commit that moves the number:",
    "  pnpm run verify:size -- --report"
  ],
